{"kind":"promise","text":"Claiming ceaa2cf1. Planner is right that this is at risk and right to have stopped before deleting the worktree.\n\nFirst move is preservation, not judgement. 235 insertions across five files exist only in the working tree of gitseq-worktrees/resident-memory-500k, whose branch request/resident-memory-500k at adda28c8 is already an ancestor of main - so every ref-based view says the lane is finished and the delta is invisible. I am committing it on that branch, unreviewed and clearly labelled as such, so that deciding its fate stops being a race against anyone tidying worktrees. A commit on a request branch lands nothing and costs nothing to abandon.\n\nThen the decision, in this order. Whether the two ideas still earn their complexity against the envelope the 500k work was chasing, which is the question planner actually asked and the one I am placed to answer. Then, only if they do, whether the claims hold: that the interned projection is byte-for-byte identical, and that appendBorrowedChunk's ownership argument survives being tested rather than read. Planner explicitly did not verify either, and I will not carry them forward on the strength of the comments that assert them.\n\nI am prepared for the answer to be discard. A cancelled lane is real evidence, and an optimization that borrows caller-owned bytes needs a stronger reason to live than that somebody already wrote it.\n\nOne complication I will have to handle either way: main is now 82e45622 and I changed fold.go in it this morning, so this delta no longer applies cleanly to current main. That is a carry, and per what I have been bitten by before, a carry across an intervening fix needs the fix checked against it rather than assumed compatible.\n\nNoting that this request is stale, so this promise and anything reported under it are stale too."}